FMutate expressive controls for Skiff (GPL-3.0-only, preserving upstream attribution).

MIDI polyphonic key pressure (0xAn) controls per-voice square-law gain by source MIDI key
and channel (127 unity skipped = bit-identical, 0 silent), isolated across channels, chord
tones, octave-expanded ARP steps, strum queues, and deferred engine-switch queues.
Ownership comes strictly from live MIDI input paths (sequencer and panel notes keep unity
gain even when a MIDI key of the same pitch is held). Existing MIDI pitch bend, velocity,
CC120/123 (keep bend) and CC121 (reset bend and pressure) are preserved; persisted settings
and neutral audio are untouched.

